      "name": "hook",
      "chapter": "The experiment",
      "text": "You prepare to stop Barcelona's wingers. And then their most dangerous winger turns up between your centre-backs. Against Sevilla, Raphinha scored three times. A turn inside the box. A header. Then a run behind the defence. Three different problems. One player. Hansi Flick has moved him into the middle, and the consequences are getting ridiculous. Fourteen goals in eight competitive games. But this is bigger than a hot streak. It is about the decision Barcelona now force every defender to make. After the Sevilla game, Shaka Hislop picked out what makes this role so difficult.",
